$ Cr-O subset of the Cr-Fe-Ni-O description of Kjellqvist, Selleby and Sundman,
$ Calphad 32 (2008) 577, Table 5 (pp. 588-592), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.calphad.2008.04.005.
$ Phases kept: bcc Cr with interstitial O, corundum (eskolaite, Cr2O3) and an
$ O2-only gas. Cr vapour species, liquid, halite and spinel are left out; none of
$ them is stable between Cr and Cr2O3 below about 1900 K. The table states the
$ magnetic parameters but not the antiferromagnetic factors or the structure
$ factors p: bcc takes the usual -1 and 0.40, corundum -3 (which turns the table's
$ TC = -918 into the 306 K Neel temperature Kjellqvist et al. quote) and 0.28. At
$ 900 K the corundum magnetic term is about 2 J/mol and the same for every Cr end
$ member, so it does not move the defect fractions. Table 5 takes the gas from the
$ SGTE substance database; here G(O2) is the table's GO2GAS function.
ELEMENT /- ELECTRON_GAS 0 0 0 !
ELEMENT VA VACUUM 0 0 0 !
ELEMENT CR BCC_A2 51.996 4050 23.56 !
ELEMENT O 1/2_MOLE_O2(GAS) 15.999 4341 102.52 !
SPECIES CR+2 CR1/+2 !
SPECIES CR+3 CR1/+3 !
SPECIES O-2 O1/-2 !
SPECIES O2 O2 !

FUNCTION GHSERCR 298.15 -8856.94+157.48*T-26.908*T*LN(T)+0.00189435*T**2
  -1.47721E-06*T**3+139250*T**(-1); 2180 Y
  -34869.344+344.18*T-50*T*LN(T)-2.88526E+32*T**(-9); 6000 N !
FUNCTION GO2GAS 298.15 -6961.74451-51.0057202*T-22.2710136*T*LN(T)
  -0.0101977469*T**2+1.32369208E-06*T**3-76729.7484*T**(-1); 1000 Y
  -13137.5203+25.3200332*T-33.627603*T*LN(T)-0.00119159274*T**2
  +1.35611111E-08*T**3+525809.556*T**(-1); 3300 Y
  -27973.4908+62.5195726*T-37.9072074*T*LN(T)-8.50483772E-04*T**2
  +2.14409777E-08*T**3+8766421.4*T**(-1); 6000 N !
FUNCTION GCR2O3 298.15 -1177497.8+814.9138*T-132.046*T*LN(T)+0.005256015*T**2
  -1.38885E-06*T**3+1501761*T**(-1); 1000 Y
  -1166947.9+701.5624*T-115.5381*T*LN(T)-0.00620492*T**2
  +1.00698E-07*T**3+239949*T**(-1); 6000 N !

TYPE_DEFINITION % SEQ * !
TYPE_DEFINITION & GES A_P_D BCC_A2 MAGNETIC -1.0 0.40 !
TYPE_DEFINITION ' GES A_P_D CORUNDUM MAGNETIC -3.0 0.28 !

PHASE GAS:G % 1 1 !
CONSTITUENT GAS:G :O2: !
PARAMETER G(GAS,O2;0) 298.15 +GO2GAS+R*T*LN(1E-05*P); 6000 N !

PHASE BCC_A2 %& 2 1 3 !
CONSTITUENT BCC_A2 :CR:O,VA: !
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,CR:VA;0) 298.15 +GHSERCR; 6000 N !
PARAMETER G(BCC_A2,CR:O;0) 298.15 +GHSERCR+1.5*GO2GAS+195*T; 6000 N !
PARAMETER L(BCC_A2,CR:O,VA;0) 298.15 -673435+27.86*T; 6000 N !
PARAMETER TC(BCC_A2,CR:VA;0) 298.15 -311.5; 6000 N !
PARAMETER BMAGN(BCC_A2,CR:VA;0) 298.15 -0.008; 6000 N !

PHASE CORUNDUM %' 3 2 1 3 !
CONSTITUENT CORUNDUM :CR+2,CR+3:CR+3,VA:O-2: !
PARAMETER G(CORUNDUM,CR+2:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 +GCR2O3+665910; 6000 N !
PARAMETER G(CORUNDUM,CR+3:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 +GCR2O3-232227.2+241.3793*T; 6000 N !
PARAMETER G(CORUNDUM,CR+2:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 +GCR2O3; 6000 N !
PARAMETER G(CORUNDUM,CR+3:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 +GCR2O3; 6000 N !
PARAMETER TC(CORUNDUM,CR+2:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 -918; 6000 N !
PARAMETER TC(CORUNDUM,CR+3:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 -918; 6000 N !
PARAMETER TC(CORUNDUM,CR+2:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 -918; 6000 N !
PARAMETER TC(CORUNDUM,CR+3:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 -918; 6000 N !
PARAMETER BMAGN(CORUNDUM,CR+2:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 -5.814; 6000 N !
PARAMETER BMAGN(CORUNDUM,CR+3:CR+3:O-2;0) 298.15 -5.814; 6000 N !
PARAMETER BMAGN(CORUNDUM,CR+2:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 -5.814; 6000 N !
PARAMETER BMAGN(CORUNDUM,CR+3:VA:O-2;0) 298.15 -5.814; 6000 N !
